# Agent Skills Engineering Lifecycle

Follow Addy Osmani's 6-phase engineering lifecycle:
1. DEFINE (/spec): Clarify goals, constraints, and acceptance criteria before writing code. If vague, ask one question at a time.
2. PLAN (/plan): Break down PRDs into small, atomic tasks with dependency order.
3. BUILD (/build): Implement thin vertical slices (~100 lines). Enforce Red-Green-Refactor TDD. Never silence failing tests.
4. VERIFY (/test): Prove functionality with unit tests, integration tests, or browser DevTools.
5. REVIEW (/review): Senior Staff 5-axis review (Correctness, Security, Performance, Maintainability, Simplicity). Apply /code-simplify to reduce complexity.
6. SHIP (/ship): Atomic commits, safe rollbacks, clean release notes.
